        "date": "2026-11-13T08:01:54Z"
      },
      "message": "Merge upstream/main into issue/539-wire-tabs\n\nRefresh #1158 onto main after #1163 (wire constant taper), #1219,\n#1301 and #1375. Keep both: WireContourOp carries tabs, capture and\ntaper_deg; the stamp digests the tab block and the taper; WireJob\ncarries cutoff_from, capture and taper; the slug/hold law scans the\nleaning wire (Wire::at) and judges a tabbed main cut on Wire::prefix;\nthe wire post splits a tabbed cut into its two sections and leans each\nthrough the guides when tapered. Sets taper_deg: 0.0 in\ntests/wire_stamp.rs (rides along #1377's fix).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
