      "message": "fix(wire): drop the duplicate taper_deg; pin the hold law's main-cut boundary\n\nAfter merging main, wire_stamp.rs stated taper_deg twice (E0062): once\nfrom main's #1378 and once from the refresh's own copy. Keep one.\n\nhold_tests::the_main_cut_ends_on_its_own_last_move pins\nWire::prefix(m + 1). In case A the main cut's last move closes the cut,\nso the tabs hold nothing. In case B the cut-off's first move closes it,\nso the tabs hold. Reading the main cut as prefix(m) or prefix(m + 2)\ngives the wrong verdict in one of the two cases.\n\nRefs #539\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
